@@ -259,6 +259,22 @@ GPU. RViz is comfortable, Gazebo is slow but usable (Apple Silicon handles it
 better than most laptops). That is the expected Path C experience; say so when
 you submit if it is unusable.
 
+### Moving the camera in Gazebo (in the browser)
+
+Gazebo's camera uses three mouse buttons: **left-drag pans, middle-drag orbits,
+right-drag or the scroll wheel zooms.** A trackpad has no middle button, and
+its two-finger scroll arrives as many tiny steps, so zooming can feel stuck.
+
+- Zoom: scroll with two fingers, slowly, and wait a moment — Gazebo only moves
+  the camera on the frames it manages to draw. Do **not** pinch; that zooms the
+  browser page, not Gazebo.
+- Try Firefox if Safari or Chrome scrolls too fast or not at all.
+- A plain USB mouse with a wheel and a middle button makes Gazebo much easier;
+  worth it for the sessions that use Gazebo.
+- If it is slow rather than stuck, lower `VNC_RESOLUTION` in `.env` (for example
+  `1024x576`), then `./lab.sh restart`, and give Docker Desktop more CPUs
+  (Settings → Resources).
+
